# The scripts and the config are POSIX sh, sourced and executed as text.
# CRLF breaks them, and not everywhere the same way, which is the worst case:
# measured 2026-11-14, a CRLF copy still runs under Git Bash's sh but dies
# under dash on its second line with "set: Illegal option -", because the
# option becomes "-u" plus a carriage return. A clone made on Windows with
# core.autocrlf=true and then used on Linux, in WSL or inside a container
# would hit exactly that.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
